                "content": "The criteria for determining if an element has at most two digits is based on the number of digits in the integer value itself. Specifically, an element has at most two digits if it is between 0 (inclusive) and 99 (inclusive). This is because a single-digit number or a two-digit number will have either 1 or 2 digits, respectively, while any number greater than 99 would have more than two digits."
